#descr "Iblis is the Father of Jinn, a being from ancient times who served a previous Pantokrator. His power was vast, and he had dominion over the wind and the flames of the sun. But he grew arrogant, dissatisfied with his lot, and sought to make children that would rival his master's creation. He first spawned the Binn and the Hinn from the Scorching Wind of Samum. Emboldened by his success, he set the desert wind aflame, imbuing it with his power, and from it wove the Jinn to life. He made the Marids, first among the Jinn, regal and mighty. Then, from what fire remained, he made the Ifrits, proud and scheming; the Shayatin, devious and cunning; the Houri, pure and exquisite. Finally, from the smouldering ashes he made the Ghuls, ravenous and cruel and without number, as the last of his creation.
The Pantokrator beheld this slight, and called Iblis sinner, and banished him to where the light of the world does not shine. For centuries he has remained trapped in this eternal prison, letting his hatred stew, plotting his revenge on the world that failed him. Now, he has returned to command the armies of his children. His power rivals that of the pretender gods, and faith falters wherever he makes himself known."
