#name "Bhöd"
#epithet "Tertön Kings"
#era 1
#descr "The Kingdom of Bhöd is a cold, mountainous land inhabited by hardy tribes and the ape-like Mi Gö. Ruled over by Tertön Kings of great wisdom the land has prospered. Sacred Lha spirits dwell in hallowed sites on the Bhöd mountain and live amongst the humans and Mi Gö. They have taught the secret of steel to the tribes and now the warriors of the Bhödpa bear fine weapons and wear scale armour. The armies of Bhöd consist of all three moeties, along with great Mammoths native to the mountains they call home.
The religion of Bhöd teaches deference to the spirits of the land and the ancestors. Shamans speak to the spirits and interpret their will to ensure prosperity for the tribes. The Tertön Kings uncover ancient wisdom which is passed down to the priests and common folk. Recently new practices including worship of the Rakshasa have begun to spread from nearby Lanka to lowland villages around the Bhöd mountains. With the coming of the new God the nation has unified and now the Bhödpa, Mi Gö and Lha spirits act as one."
#summary "Race: Humans, Lha spirits and ape-like Mi Gö. Prefers cold 2.
Military: Stealthy Bhödpa light infantry, horse and yak cavalry, sacred Lha and Mi Gö warriors.
Magic: Access to all elemental paths except fire, plus nature, death and some blood. A variety of summonable creatures.
Priests: Moderately strong; most priests are also mages."
#brief "The Bhöd Kingdom is a mountain nation. The tribesmen of the Bhöd mountain kingdom and the Mi Gö, descendants of an ancient race, fight alongside sacred Lha spirits."
