#selectnation 189
#uwbuild 1
#name "Fennoscandia"
#epithet "Souls of the Land"
#era 1
#descr "Fennoscandia is a harsh and frozen land inhabited by numerous tribes. In recent times both the Vanir and the Chudes have encroached on these lands, causing the disparate tribes to unite against a common foe. The wild Fenni, hardy Sami and pastoral Finnaithae have set aside their differences and pacts have been made with the Troldfolk living in the deep forests. Many such tribes shun civilization and can be recruited without the need for a permanent settlement. Iron is a sign of prestige and most warriors are lightly armored.
In Fennoscandia natural objects and animals have powerful souls and are venerated. Shamanic priests speak with the souls of beasts and the dead and are accompanied in battle by protective spirits. Ancestor spirits tied to landmarks known as Seita are worshipped and consulted in all matters. With the coming of the Awakening God the nation has found renewed purpose, as the tribes unite to reclaim their homeland."
#summary "Race: Humans and Trolls.  Prefers Cold Scale +2
Military: Light infantry and archers, stealthy archers, trolls. Many recruits not requiring a fort, with sacred Elk warriors and armored trolls in the capital.
Magic: Air, Water, Death, Nature, and Earth, a very small amount of Glamour. Most mages are spellsingers.
Priests: Average, Spirit animals may appear to defend them in battles"
#brief "Fennoscandia is a tribal nation of fierce nomadic warriors and coastal tribes. They can recruit warriors in most terrains, however they are lightly armoured. Their alliance with the troldfolk tribes provides strong troll recruits."
