#name "Rotterland"
#epithet "The Flooded Country"
#flag "rotterland/rflag.tga"
#color 0.95 0.58 0
#descr "Rotterland is a muddy lowland, where the sun neither warms you, nor dries the damp from your cloak. Once it was green and prosperous. Ostlem, the capital, was a center of trade known for its beautiful windmills and tulips. After a terrible flood in which thousands drowned or perished from famine and disease Marignon's tercios conquered Rotterland. For long years blood was mixed with mud as the people struggled to push the invaders from their country. In the final battle, Ostlem was besieged. For three years the city was bombarded with fire and lightning until only the walls still stood. Finally, the last line of defense gave and Marignese pikemen surged over the walls. Suddenly the gate of the dike was opened, and an army of mermen flooded through the breach. The Marignese either fell under the sword or drowned in their trenches and mines. Ostlem was utterly destroyed, but Rotterland was free again. The armies of Rotterland use crossbows and plate armor. Their troops are accustomed to swamplands and are resistant to disease. Under the sea they can recruit mermen to aid them."
#summary "Race: Human, disease-resistant and accustomed to living in swamps. Some Mermen allies.
Military: Arbalestiers & crossbows, average melee troops.
Magic: Water, earth, nature and death. Some air.
Priests: Stealthy
Sailing: All commanders can sail. Only Schippers can transport troops."
#brief "Rotterland is a nation of fens and swamplands allied with merfolk. Their military is quite advanced and uses plate armor and crossbows extensively. The Levee Masters are skilled in water, earth and nature whilst skilled Doctors practice death magic."
