#descr "When Sauromatia fell to Ermorian conquest the surviving tribes retreated in disarray. Some escaped to the vast grasslands of the northern steppes, allying with the local Tatar tribes and accepting the rule of their Khans. This alliance of tribes has since grown to become the Empire of Tartary. The armies of Tartary consist mainly of mounted warriors, with the bow and lance being favoured weapons. With the awakening of the True God the Golden Horde have now been roused to action. Streams of fierce steppes warriors pour down from the grasslands and the civilized nations of the world tremble in fear.
The Tatars revere the souls of their ancestors and sacred Shamanic priestesses interpret the will of the dead to aid the living. Lesser tribal shamans commune with spirits of the land and the eternal sky. The steppes people are unusually tolerant of foreign faiths, preferring to incorporate their worship into the empire. Captured temples will be converted rather than destroyed."
#summary "Race: Human
Military: Powerful mounted warriors, many archers and armored cataphracts. Many units can be recruited without a fort.
Magic: Death, Air, Nature, Earth, some Astral.
Priests: Average"
#brief "Tartary is a nation of mounted nomadic warriors with many archers and cavalry. They do not rely on permanent settlements and are highly mobile."
