#selectnation 206 -- Dirgen, Abyssal Kingdoms
#clear
#era 2
#name "Dirgen"
#epithet "Abyssal Kingdoms"
#descr "After the fall of the Basalt City, most Atlantians turned to shallower waters and built a new city of coral, but some remained in the deeps. Across the vast and seemingly inhospitable regions of the abyssal plain on the ocean floor, minor Atlantian kingdoms are emerging. In the abyssal plains of Dirgen, a field of decay littered with the countless bones of dead fish and leviathan alike, stands the largest of these kingdoms. Its rulership is claimed by the Kurvant, mages from the time of the Basalt City.
Although the secrets to crafting them have been lost, enchanted basalt weapons and armor may still be found in deep trenches and basalt ruins. The Kurvant are eager to reclaim these ancient relics for the upcoming war. Among the bones of these ocean depths a cult of death has gained prevalence, practicing necromancy towards an end known only to them. Even so, their power is undeniable and both the Kurvant and lesser kingdoms are quick to make use of it.
Now, the kingdom of Dirgen is ready to claim the ocean floor and unite the fractured deep Atlantians under the rule of the coming God."

#summary "Race: Deep Atlantians
Military: Abyssal Ones, undead fish
Magic: Death, Water, Earth, with some Fire and Astral
Priests: Weak, better priests in Basalt Cities
Mechanics: Can create new Basalt Cities in forts, enabling some capital recruits. Death and Growth scales have half the effect on pop growth."
#brief "Dirgen is a Kingdom of Deep Ones in the ocean's abyssal plains, seeking to claim the legacy of the Basalt City of Atlantis. A cult of death has emerged in the abyss, capable of raising the remains of dead leviathan. Ancient Basalt Cities are being rebuilt and their weapons used once again."
